Wow.  That is an ancient proposal.  It sounds interesting.  Whatever
happened to it?  I can see in my copy of the cll that it didn't get adopted
yet it seems to be getting use in the real world.

Guess I'll just keep in mind that sometimes people will say gi'e and
sometimes they'll say gije. Likewise for ge vs jegi.

Unless someone tries to redefine ge/gi'e is there really any collision
between the two usages anyway?
